# Correctness over performance

Read `plan.MD` before making changes. It is the authoritative current implementation plan; `roadmap.md` contains future work and must not be used as an alternative active queue.

The active stream is the lossless syntax-cutover stabilization described in `plan.MD`. Correctness, full file accounting, recovery safety, and reproducible evidence precede optimization. Do not start later CST-analysis, PHPStan-coverage, CLI, editor-latency, or comparable-performance roadmap work unless the user explicitly changes priority.

Use neutral reduced fixtures and clean controls for every correction. Do not copy private corpus source into the repository. Update `plan.MD` status only after the relevant validation exists.
